{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1415945-tron-in-storypath","id":1415945,"title":"Tron in Storypath","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-09-28T23:42:31-07:00","id":1415945,"title":"Tron in Storypath","content":"As IT nerd, I'm all for Tron movie franchise. With Tron 3 coming, I'm reading for some gaming in Storypath. How would you make Tron setting with Trinity?<br /> <br /> Graphics effects of movie 1 &amp; 2 for bonus \ud83d\ude0e <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PZ7SevBiT5s\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PZ7SevBiT5s</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-29T00:06:03-07:00","id":1415946,"title":"","content":"Tron is a fun concept, as most of the characters are no more than small programs running on a mainframe. They are not even complex programs. Yet it\u2019s awesome the way it is portrayed in the original movie, with the actor that played the programmer also played the program, and how the OS is portrayed as a tyrannical over mind with programs being used by the OS to different ends than the original programming. Except by the guy going into the computer, it\u2019s the most interesting metaphor to explain how a computer system works with no programming language or anything like that. At least for a multi terminal system.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I would make programs as simple antagonists (simple as \u201cfocused on a single\u201d, not as \u201cweek\u201d), each one good on their jobs and basically useless in other tasks. The characters themselves are humans digitalized, so they are as complex as needed, and would have some \u201cuser powers\u201d, like understanding how the system works, having access to different information or even hacking.<br /> <br /> How user powers works is another thing, I would probably go with acting the procedural, letting the characters use paths and other skills in place of the hacking and information access regular rolls. Hard to tell any other detail, must think more...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-29T00:55:42-07:00","id":1415949,"title":"","content":"In times of <b>Tron</b> (2) <b>Legacy</b> premiere ( 2010 ) I was preparing to run d20 system based on the idea - <a href=\"https://www.rpg.net/reviews/archive/13/13079.phtml\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Horizon: </b></a><b><a href=\"https://www.rpg.net/reviews/archive/13/13079.phtml\" target=\"_blank\">Virtual</a></b>. It's base premise is that characters are humans in computer or basic program types, based on fundamental d20 stats - Strength, Dexterity, Constitution, Wisdom, Intelligence, Charisma, each own type - that are infected by AI virus, becoming sentient programs themselves ( i.e. Players Characters ). Some food for thought for the Storypath setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}